=== Text #17 ===
> CTI allows a[ computer] to interact with the telephone, e.g. in setting up and terminating calls with numbers taken from a directory via a PC application.
The computer (e.g. a PC located at the same desk as the telephone) directly interacts with the telephone (First Party CTI).
The computer (could also be a co-located PC) interacts with the telephone system (e.g. SIP application server), and the latter controls the telephone: Third Party CTI.
Many OpenStage and optiPoint telephones are able to use CTI, like OpenStage 80 (Third Party) or OpenStage 40 T (First Party).
Mit CTI kann ein PC mit dem Telefon kommunizieren, z. B. zum Aufbau oder Beenden von Telefonverbindungen. Gewählt können die Rufnummern aus einem Adressbuch auf dem PC, z. B. Microsoft Outlook, werden.
Ein PC (z. B. ein Arbeitsplatzrechner neben dem Telefon) kommuniziert direkt mit dem Telefon (First Party CTI).
Ein Rechner kommuniziert mit einem Telefonsystem (z. B. SIP application server) und dieser steuert das Telefon (Third Party CTI).
Viele OpenStage- und optiPoint-Telefone sind fähig, CTI zu nutzen, z. B. OpenStage 80 (Third Party) oder OpenStage 40 T (First Party).
This page was last edited on 21 November 2013, at 12:21.[]

=== Text #18 ===
> 3CX has a Wallboard showing data from one or[ several] queues. We made our JEDWare Custom Wallboard that can show several queues and the queues Agent status for[ each] of the[ queues] on one Wallboard Screen. Our Wallboard is perfect for Call and Contact centers that maintain calls from several sources, and is a great tool for companies that wants to see what is going on in real time. Our Wallboard runs in real time, and can track all[ queues] in your 3CX Phonesystem. The Wallboard shows real time incoming and ongoing calls, and shows every agent in the specific[ queue]’s status. The Wallboard resets its data every day, or per user wish.
JEDWare wallboard shows all agents for the queues selected.[ Agents] in every[ queue will] show their current status, and show different status for inbound/outbound calls. If an[ agent]’s soft phone/computer is turned off, the wallboard will also indicate this. The Wallboard offers a quick way for agents to see who is either in their current[ queue] or to see what agents are currently busy.
JEDWare wallboard has a customizable design. This means you can choose how you want your wallboard to look. You can add more queues, choose when the SLA statistics turn red. You can even change what queues should be bigger than the[ others]. Because of this, the system will always suit your company, You can view the status of up to 12 Que[ues] at the same time and change the display, for example, if[ a queue] has more agents than[ others]. This allows your JEDWare wallboard to always be used for the amount of Queues you have, whether it's few or many.[][][]

